---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Projects - Steve Wang"
  description="Selected projects by Steve Wang, including digital signage CMS work, Fuel Tracker, the Shared Bill expense app, Project Status Hub, and purchasing workflow tooling."
  current="projects"
>
  <main>
    <section class="page-title section-wrap">
      <h1>Projects</h1>
      <p>
        Selected work across full-stack product development, live personal software,
        private operations dashboards, and purchasing workflow automation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-wrap project-list">
      <article class="detail-card" id="digital-signage-cms">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Full-stack product</span>
            <h2>Digital Signage CMS</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Production work</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Scope</h3>
            <p>Production CMS for digital signage content, screens, assets, templates, editing, permissions, billing, and deployment workflows.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Owned Work</h3>
            <p>Permission control, Stripe payment setup, related CMS flows, CI/CD pipeline work, backend APIs, database changes, and production support.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Also Supported</h3>
            <p>CRM sync, screen monitoring notifications, Electron support, and Android/Tizen TV app maintenance.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>React, TypeScript, Node.js, MySQL, Stripe API, Ontraport CRM, Docker, Nginx, CircleCI, Bitbucket Pipelines, AWS EC2.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="fuel-tracker">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Personal product</span>
            <h2>Fuel Tracker</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Private release</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Problem</h3>
            <p>Off-the-shelf fuel apps felt heavy and missed wanted features, so refill records never stayed consistent.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Solution</h3>
            <p>A personal fuel logging app with AI receipt extraction, shipped two ways: a cloud web app and a portable Windows desktop build, with English/Chinese UI and separate region, currency, and unit settings.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>AI Extraction</h3>
            <p>A serverless function reads receipt photos into litres, pump unit price, retail total, fuel grade, brand, station name, and purchase datetime, covering Australian and Chinese receipt formats, with per-account token usage visible in settings.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>React, TypeScript, Vite, Vitest, Electron portable build, AWS Amplify Hosting, Cognito auth, AppSync/DynamoDB data, Lambda receipt extraction.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-strip" aria-label="Fuel Tracker screenshots">
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/fueltracker-overview.png" alt="Fuel Tracker overview showing consumption, cost, distance, and recent activity." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Overview metrics and recent activity</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/fueltracker-ai-entry.png" alt="Fuel Tracker add-fill screen showing AI receipt extraction filling fuel details." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>AI-assisted receipt entry</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="shared-bill">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Personal web app</span>
            <h2>Shared Bill</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Private release</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Purpose</h3>
            <p>Hosted app for recording shared expenses, splitting costs, and calculating who should pay whom.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Hosted Web App</h3>
            <p>Supabase-backed sign-in, groups with member roles and invites, weighted expense splits, settlement calculation, completed transfer tracking, and English/Chinese UI. Settlement details export as a shareable PNG image.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Import Path</h3>
            <p>Owner-only desktop JSON import keeps the original Electron data path useful while moving shared records into the hosted backend.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>React, Vite, TypeScript, Supabase Auth and Postgres with row-level security, AWS Amplify Hosting, Electron, shared settlement core, and Vitest unit/UI tests.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-strip" aria-label="Shared Bill screenshots">
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/sharebill-expenses.png" alt="Shared Bill expenses tab with an add-expense form and a list of recorded expenses showing payer, amount, and participants." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Expense entry with participant selection</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/sharebill-settlement.png" alt="Shared Bill settlement tab showing a minimal transfer plan and a per-person paid, shared, and net balance table." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Settlement plan and per-person balances</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="project-status-hub">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Private dashboard</span>
            <h2>Project Status Hub</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Owner-only</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Purpose</h3>
            <p>Private operations dashboard for personal web projects, covering deploy health, uptime, provider status, collector errors, aggregate usage, and month-to-date cost.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Collectors</h3>
            <p>Nine provider adapters — HTTP health, Amplify deploy status, AWS Cost Explorer, Supabase aggregates and health, Resend email health, OpenAI usage, GitHub Actions CI/usage, and Cloudflare domains — run on a scheduled GitHub Action and write append-only snapshots.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Access Model</h3>
            <p>Frontend login gates the dashboard before data renders, Supabase RLS allows reads only for approved dashboard users, and collectors store aggregate signals only — never raw app records.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>React, Vite, TypeScript, Supabase Auth with row-level security, scheduled GitHub Actions collectors, AWS Amplify Hosting, and Vitest with mocked provider tests.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-strip" aria-label="Project Status Hub screenshots">
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/statushub-overview.png" alt="Project Status Hub overview showing tracked apps, health summary, month-to-date cost, and per-app deploy and uptime status cards." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Overview with per-app health and cost</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/statushub-collectors.png" alt="Project Status Hub collector diagnostics table listing provider runs, durations, and health status for each collector." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Collector diagnostics across providers</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="purchasing-workflow-tools">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Current focus</span>
            <h2>Purchasing Workflow Tools</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">In progress</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Goal</h3>
            <p>Speed up low-stock ordering decisions that are possible in Excel but slow to prepare and check by hand.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Current Tool</h3>
            <p>Python import flow for item, sales, cost, price, and supplier data with automatic order amount calculation.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Rules</h3>
            <p>Uses supplier MOQ, layer price, pallet price, and packaging constraints when calculating suggested order amounts.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>Python first. Future UI will depend on the workflow shape after the calculation model is stable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
